cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "PeerReviewAgents"
abstract: >-
  PeerReviewAgents produces an evidence-linked peer review of a manuscript PDF.
  One command imports the PDF locally into immutable source blocks with
  evidence handles, runs independent reviewers against bounded manuscript and
  literature tools, and synthesizes their findings through an audited debate in
  which every original finding must be retained, merged, rejected with reasons,
  or sent for verification. Every finding carries the source block it is
  anchored to and the exact quotation it rests on; a quotation that does not
  match the manuscript is quarantined rather than reported. Reviews run on a
  signed-in Claude Code or Codex subscription and make no API-key calls. Each
  run records its manuscript manifest, tool logs, coverage record, and model
  usage, and the reports are written from that saved JSON without further
  inference, so a stopped or blocked run still reports what it produced. The
  command line, a local web UI, an MCP server, and plugins for local coding
  agents all run the same review. The system is research software for review
  assistance and evaluation, not a substitute for accountable editorial
  judgment.
type: software
